=== Introduction
--- The Epistles Placed in the Book of Acts [title]
overline: Bible lessons
heading: The Epistles Placed in the Book of Acts
sub: List of the Epistles placed in the context of Acts chapters where they were most likely written (based on a conservative, fundamentalist timeline aligning with Acts events).
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move through the lesson. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

=== Acts, chapter by chapter
--- Acts, Chapter by Chapter
kicker: The Epistles against the chapters of Acts
image: lessons/bible/bible-epistles-placed-in-acts.svg | The 28 chapters of Acts drawn as a column, with James beside Acts 1-12, Galatians beside Acts 13-14, 1 and 2 Thessalonians beside Acts 15-18, 1 Corinthians beside Acts 19, 2 Corinthians beside Acts 20:1-2, Romans beside Acts 20:3-38, Acts 21-28 marked as Paul’s arrest, trials, and journey to Rome, and the Prison Epistles (Ephesians, Colossians, Philemon, Philippians) after Acts 28. | Each epistle beside the chapters of Acts where it was most likely written.

=== Reading through Acts
--- Reading Through Acts (1 of 2)
kicker: Reading through Acts
step: Acts 1-12 | Read **James** (written ~AD 44–49 from Jerusalem, addressing early persecution and trials among dispersed Jewish believers)
step: Acts 13-14 | Read **Galatians** (written ~AD 48–49 from Antioch, shortly after the first missionary journey to the Galatian churches)
step: Acts 15-18 | Read **1 Thessalonians** and **2 Thessalonians** (written ~AD 50–51 from Corinth, to encourage the new church planted in Thessalonica during the second journey)
step: Acts 19 | Read **1 Corinthians** (written ~AD 55 from Ephesus, addressing issues in the Corinthian church)

--- Reading Through Acts (2 of 2)
kicker: Reading through Acts
step: Acts 20:1-2 | Read **2 Corinthians** (written ~AD 56 from Macedonia, as a follow-up to 1 Corinthians)
step: Acts 20:3-38 | Read **Romans** (written ~AD 57 from Corinth, as Paul planned his trip to Rome)
step: Acts 21-28 | Paul’s arrest, trials, and journey to Rome
step: After Acts 28 | Read the Prison Epistles: **Ephesians**, **Colossians**, **Philemon**, and **Philippians** (written ~AD 60–62 from house arrest in Rome)

=== After Acts
--- Post-Acts Epistles
kicker: After Acts ends ~AD 62
table: Epistle | Written
tr: **1 Timothy** and **Titus** | ~AD 63–65
tr: **2 Timothy** | ~AD 66–67
tr: **Hebrews** | ~AD 60–68, possibly from Italy
tr: **1 Peter** | ~AD 62–63, from Rome/“Babylon”
tr: **2 Peter** | ~AD 65–68
tr: **Jude** | ~AD 65–80
tr: **1 John**, **2 John**, **3 John** and **Revelation** | ~AD 85–95

